        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="d388-3" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d388-3"/>

                <head>389. Telegram 1330 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d389-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-11-29">November 29, 1955, 7:34
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d389-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d389-1"/>
                <p>1330. For Johnson.</p>
                <p>UNC called meeting of MAC November 26 at which US representative referred to
                        Wang statement Geneva that MAC was
                    proper channel for accounting for missing US military personnel and said US
                    concurred this view. He presented revised list 2720 UN personnel including 450
                    US servicemen and offered individual accounting for 98,739 personnel of
                    Communist side whenever Communists presented accounting for UN personnel.
                    Communist side accepted lists but stated (1) individuals held outside Korea do
                    not come under authority MAC and therefore irrelevant to discuss in MAC; (2) MAC
                    has no connection with POW’s disposed of by PRC. Also noted UNC offer to account
                    for Communist side personnel and stated it unnecessary comment on UNC list at
                    this time.</p>
                <p>In view above MAC action you need not raise this subject again with Wang until further instructed. However,
                    Communist statements <pb facs="0593" n="546" type="typeset" xml:id="pg546"/> 1
                    and 2 above provide opening resume negotiation with Wang if Communists give no satisfaction in MAC within reasonable
                    time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
